\n- Improved Routing\r\n- PSR-0 and composer support.\r\n- Simpler configuration and bootstrapping.\r\n- Improved configuration handling.\r\n- Improved bake.\r\n\r\nSee [the roadmap](http://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/wiki/3.0-roadmap) for more details.","creator":null,"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":2464,"state":"closed","created_at":"2013-10-11T20:56:23Z","updated_at":"2015-12-17T03:00:48Z","due_on":"2015-03-22T04:00:00Z","closed_at":"2015-03-23T01:02:41Z"},"comments":4,"created_at":"2014-11-19T17:04:25Z","updated_at":"2014-12-24T12:02:33Z","closed_at":"2014-12-24T12:02:33Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Trying to build something like this....\n\n``` php\n// Query\n$Query->where(function ($expr) use ($field, $value1, $value2, $Query) {\n    $field = $Query->func()->left([$field, '32' => 'literal']);\n    return $expr\n        ->lte($field, substr($value1, 0, 32))\n        ->gte($field, substr($value2, 0, 32));\n});\n\n// Resulting dump\n'sql' => 'SELECT ... WHERE ((left(:c0, :c1)) <= :c2 AND (left(:c3, :c4)) >= :c5)',\n'params' => [\n    ':c0' => [\n        'value' => 'field',\n        'type' => null,\n        'placeholder' => 'c0'\n    ],\n    ':c1' => [\n        'value' => 'literal',\n        'type' => null,\n        'placeholder' => 'c1'\n    ],\n    ':c2' => [\n        'value' => '...',\n        'type' => null,\n        'placeholder' => 'c2'\n    ],\n    ':c3' => [\n        'value' => 'field',\n        'type' => null,\n        'placeholder' => 'c3'\n    ],\n    ':c4' => [\n        'value' => 'literal',\n        'type' => null,\n        'placeholder' => 'c4'\n    ],\n    ':c5' => [\n        'value' => '...',\n        'type' => null,\n        'placeholder' => 'c5'\n    ]\n]\n```\n\nThe [FunctionExpression](https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/3.0/src/Database/Expression/FunctionExpression.php#L95) class checks if the `$k` is a string and if value `=== 'literal'` which in this case it actually is however `debug(is_string('32'));` will return `true`. I also have trouble generating SQL similar to `CAST(SUBSTRING(field, 32) AS SIGNED)` because I can't overload the [`$conjunction`](https://github.com/cakephp/cakephp/blob/3.0/src/Database/Expression/QueryExpression.php#L65) option. I'm not sure if this is an _official_ issue as it does kind of seem like a grey area of me just making my own `CastExpression` class but I kind of felt like the literal was an issue.\n","closed_by":{"login":"lorenzo","id":37621,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjIx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37621?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo","html_url":"https://github.com/lorenzo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lorenzo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/5211/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cakephp/cakephp/issues/5211/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}